        /// <summary>
        /// Initiate a scroll session for retrieving large product datasets.
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// Bulk extraction endpoint — full-catalog syncs (PIM, ERP, marketplace), exports,
        /// <br/>search-index reindexing. Also required past the 10,000 offset cap on POST /Query.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>Returns a `scrollId` and the first batch. Pass `scrollId` to
        /// <br/>GET /api/products/Query/Scroll/{scrollId} until it comes back null. Sessions expire after
        /// <br/>10 minutes of inactivity; per-tenant concurrency is capped.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>Same filter set as POST /Query (see request schema) and identical response shape — price
        /// <br/>context filtering, inventory cleanup and property-list shaping apply on both the initial
        /// <br/>batch and continuations. `savedSearchId` works here too (bulk-extract a saved search); the
        /// <br/>saved search is resolved once at initiation, so edits to it never affect an active scroll.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>### Default values are omitted
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>To keep responses small, a field is left out when it holds its default value: `false`, `0`,
        /// <br/>`null`, the empty date `0001-01-01T00:00:00`, the empty id
        /// <br/>`00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000`, or an enum's first value. **A missing field means
        /// <br/>that value, not "unknown".** `""` and `[]` are real values and are always returned.
        /// <br/>            
