        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**2. Filtered list with a tight payload** (recommended). Order lines are usually the bulk
        /// <br/>of the document — exclude them when you only need header data.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "take": 50,
        /// <br/>  "page": 1,
        /// <br/>  "statuses": ["Sent"],
        /// <br/>  "storeIds": ["store-1"],
        /// <br/>  "sort": [{ "field": "created", "direction": "desc" }],
        /// <br/>  "fields": { "exclude": ["purchaseOrderForm.lineItems"] }
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**3. Only the fields you need.** The document `id` is always returned.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "supplierId": "SUPPLIER-1",
        /// <br/>  "fields": { "include": ["purchaseOrderNumber", "status", "total"] }
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// </remarks>
