        /// <summary>
        /// Query products. Returns full product models with explicit control over market, store, and customer context.
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// Primary endpoint for fetching products: single-product lookups, filtered lists, and
        /// <br/>paginated UI queries. Pagination is capped at offset (Take * Page) of 10,000 — past that,
        /// <br/>use POST /api/products/Query/Scroll.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>All filter fields are documented on the request schema below.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>### Default values are omitted
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>To keep responses small, a field is left out when it holds its default value: `false`, `0`,
        /// <br/>`null`, the empty date `0001-01-01T00:00:00`, the empty id
        /// <br/>`00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000`, or an enum's first value. **A missing field means
        /// <br/>that value, not "unknown".** `""` and `[]` are real values and are always returned.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>A field marked `nullable` in the schema has `null` as its default, so it is left out only
        /// <br/>when it is null — a nullable boolean holding `false`, or a nullable number holding `0`, is
        /// <br/>still returned.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>For the full reference, the ID-lookup matrix, and response-size guidance, see
        /// <br/>https://docs.omnium.no/docs/Integrations/product-query.
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>### Examples
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**1. Single product with market pricing.** The simplest case — one product, prices filtered
        /// <br/>to one market.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "productIds": ["PROD-123"],
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"]
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**2. Single product with market pricing and tight payload** (recommended). Same as above
        /// <br/>but only the fields you actually need. Variants come back with just `skuId` and `size` —
        /// <br/>every other variant field is stripped. Cart pickers, barcode reverse-lookups, detail views.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "productIds": ["PROD-123"],
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"],
        /// <br/>  "fields": { "include": ["productId", "name", "prices", "variants.skuId", "variants.size"] }
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**3. Category list page.** Paginated browse with market context and a tight response —
        /// <br/>the canonical product-list-in-a-UI pattern.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "take": 50,
        /// <br/>  "page": 1,
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"],
        /// <br/>  "productCategoryIds": ["CAT-summer-clothing"],
        /// <br/>  "isActive": true,
        /// <br/>  "fields": { "include": ["productId", "name", "prices", "mainImageUrl", "variants.skuId"] }
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**4. Raw product lookup — all prices, no context filtering.** Use `includeAllPrices: true`
        /// <br/>to bypass price-context filtering while keeping product-availability filtering. Useful for
        /// <br/>price management UIs and audits where you need every price for a product, not just the
        /// <br/>market/store/customer-relevant ones.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "productIds": ["PROD-123"],
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"],
        /// <br/>  "includeAllPrices": true
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**5. Price context — scope prices independently of availability.** Top-level fields filter which
        /// <br/>products are returned; `priceContext` controls which prices come back (and how they sort). Each
        /// <br/>`priceContext` field overrides its top-level counterpart for pricing only — anything left out
        /// <br/>falls back to the top-level value, so the common case needs no `priceContext` at all. Store
        /// <br/>groups and additional price stores live here only (they never filter products). Below: products
        /// <br/>available in `SWE`, priced for the `SWE` market *and* the `MiraklSellers` store group, club
        /// <br/>prices included.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["SWE"],
        /// <br/>  "productParentIds": ["354931"],
        /// <br/>  "isCustomerClubMember": true,
        /// <br/>  "priceContext": { "storeGroupIds": ["MiraklSellers"] }
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**6. Saved search as the base query.** Run a saved product search (created in the Omnium UI)
        /// <br/>and override parts of it per request. The saved search supplies the filters; any field set on
        /// <br/>the request replaces the saved value for that field. Pagination, sorting (when given) and
        /// <br/>field selection always come from the request. Price context is never taken from the saved
        /// <br/>search — pass market/store/customer context explicitly to scope prices, as below.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "savedSearchId": "0e3c9c9b-7b53-4c8e-9f2a-1f5d3f0a1234",
        /// <br/>  "take": 50,
        /// <br/>  "page": 1,
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"],
        /// <br/>  "sort": [{ "field": "name", "direction": "asc" }]
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>**7. Search group as membership.** Run a search group (created in the Omnium UI) as membership
        /// <br/>ANDed with this request. Extra filters on the request AND with membership; they do not replace
        /// <br/>member saved-search fields. Mutually exclusive with `savedSearchId`. An unknown id is rejected with 400.
        /// <br/>```json
        /// <br/>{
        /// <br/>  "searchGroupId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
        /// <br/>  "take": 50,
        /// <br/>  "page": 1,
        /// <br/>  "marketIds": ["NOR"],
        /// <br/>  "productCategoryIds": ["CAT-summer-clothing"]
        /// <br/>}
        /// <br/>```
        /// <br/>            
        /// <br/>Image and asset URLs follow the first entry of the top-level `marketIds` (the availability
        /// <br/>market): when the tenant has per-market CDN settings, that market's CDN host is used.
        /// <br/>`priceContext` never affects asset URLs — it scopes prices only.
        /// </remarks>
        /// <param name="body">Query request with filters, market/store context, pagination, and field selection</param>
        /// <returns>Query successful</returns>
